---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { ANALYTICS_ENABLED } from '../consts';
---
<BaseLayout title="Privacy" description="What stays in your browser and what is sent to a service when you use SOFT CAT .ai.">
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 py-16">
    <header class="mb-10">
      <a href="/" class="font-mono text-sm text-text-muted hover:text-neon-cyan mb-4 inline-block">← home</a>
      <h1 class="font-mono text-3xl font-bold text-text-bright">Privacy</h1>
      <p class="text-text-muted mt-3">Updated 13 September 2026</p>
    </header>
    <div class="space-y-8 text-text-primary leading-relaxed">
      <p>SOFT CAT is a static site with browser tools and a few external services. Here is where data goes.</p>
      <section>
        <h2 class="font-mono text-lg text-neon-green mb-3">Calculators and editors</h2>
        <p>Token estimates, prompt comparisons and JSON validation run in your browser. These tools do not send the text you enter to a model. Prompt Workbench saves versions in this browser's local storage when you choose Save. Clearing site data removes those saved prompts. You can download and import a library backup.</p>
        <p class="mt-3">Opening a Workbench draft in Chat Playground puts the filled system prompt, user message and model choice in this tab's session storage. The playground accepts a transfer for up to 30 minutes and removes it when read. Importing a draft does not send a model request.</p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2 class="font-mono text-lg text-neon-cyan mb-3">Chat Playground</h2>
        <p>When you send a message, your browser sends your API key to OpenRouter for authentication. Your messages, system prompt and conversation history go to OpenRouter and the model provider it routes to. Their processing and retention policies apply. Provider charges may apply to your account.</p>
        <p class="mt-3">The key stays in memory for this page unless you choose “Remember key on this device”. That option saves it in local storage. You can clear a saved key from the playground. Conversations are kept in page memory and disappear on reload.</p>
        <p class="mt-3"><a href="https://openrouter.ai/privacy" class="text-neon-cyan underline underline-offset-4">OpenRouter privacy policy</a></p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2 class="font-mono text-lg text-neon-purple mb-3">Page delivery and analytics</h2>
        <p><a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement" class="text-neon-cyan underline underline-offset-4">GitHub Pages</a> hosts the site and may retain request logs. Fonts load from Google Fonts, so your browser makes requests to Google's servers.</p>
        {ANALYTICS_ENABLED ? <p class="mt-3">Cloudflare Web Analytics is enabled for aggregate usage information. It uses a beacon request and does not set analytics cookies. See <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/web-analytics/" class="text-neon-cyan underline underline-offset-4">Cloudflare's explanation</a>.</p> : <p class="mt-3">The analytics beacon is disabled in this build.</p>}
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2 class="font-mono text-lg text-neon-amber mb-3">Email subscription</h2>
        <p>The Dispatch form sends the email address you submit to Buttondown to manage the subscription. See <a href="https://buttondown.com/legal/privacy" class="text-neon-cyan underline underline-offset-4">Buttondown's privacy policy</a>. Unsubscribe using the link in an email.</p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2 class="font-mono text-lg text-text-bright mb-3">Contact</h2>
        <p>Questions? Email <a href="mailto:workshop@softcat.ai" class="text-neon-cyan underline underline-offset-4">workshop@softcat.ai</a>.</p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
